<p id="mwAw"><i id="mwBA"><b id="mwBQ">Solar Energy Materials and Solar Cells</b></i> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Scientific_journal" title="Scientific journal" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBg">scientific journal</a>  published by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Elsevier" title="Elsevier" id="mwBw">Elsevier</a> covering research related to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Solar_energy" title="Solar energy" id="mwCA">solar energy</a> materials and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Solar_cells" title="Solar cells" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCQ">solar cells</a>. According to the <i id="mwCg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Journal_Citation_Reports" title="Journal Citation Reports" id="mwCw">Journal Citation Reports</a></i>, <i id="mwDA">Solar Energy Materials and Solar Cells</i> has a 2020 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Impact_factor" title="Impact factor" id="mwDQ">impact factor</a> of 7.267.<sup about="#mwt5" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-WoS_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"WoS"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WoS-1"}}'><a href="./Solar_Energy_Materials_and_Solar_Cells#cite_note-WoS-1" id="mwDg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}' id="mwEg"/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwEw"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Controversies">Controversies</h2>
<p id="mwFA">A paper titled "Ageing effects of perovskite solar cells under different environmental factors and electrical load conditions" published in 2018 in the journal<sup about="#mwt10" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="./Solar_Energy_Materials_and_Solar_Cells#cite_note-2" id="mwFQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGA">]</span></span></a></sup> corresponded to a paper previously published in the journal <i id="mwGQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Nature_Energy" title="Nature Energy" id="mwGg">Nature Energy</a></i> as "Systematic investigation of the impact of operation conditions on the degradation behaviour of perovskite solar cells".<sup about="#mwt13" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="./Solar_Energy_Materials_and_Solar_Cells#cite_note-3" id="mwGw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">]</span></span></a></sup>
It led to an investigation of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Plagiarism" title="Plagiarism" id="mwHw">plagiarism</a>.<sup about="#mwt16" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="./Solar_Energy_Materials_and_Solar_Cells#cite_note-4" id="mwIA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

